  "sources": {
    "readme": "README.md",
    "readme_excerpt": [
      "1. validates the URL, port, crawl scope, and URL-length budget; 2. reserves the global request/origin budget; 3. obtains the exact origin's rate and in-flight permit; 4. resolves through a shared timeout-bounded resolver and rejects denied CIDRs; 5. sends exactly one HTTP request and charges streamed bytes to the crawl; 6. records status, Retry-After, timing",
      "Redirect targets repeat the page-scope and robots checks before being requested. Retries repeat the origin-scheduler acquisition. The default redirect policy is withincrawlscope, HTTPS downgrades are denied, the default scope is the seed's exact origin, only ports 80 and 443 are enabled, and IANA non-global address classes are denied."
    ],
